  story:[ "<b>The crossing lamps are dark behind police tape.</b> A relay cabinet stands open, and a temporary strap hangs from two numbered terminals.", "S&T Tech Mara Doss, The Signaller, and The Clerk can reconstruct the route from track equipment through the panel to the deferred fault record.", "The railway is arguing between <b>Sabotage — something left on the line</b> and <b>Simple driver error — a signal run by</b>. Both conclusions skip the logic that should have made the movement impossible.", "The line is scheduled to reopen in eight days under temporary working. Every alteration after that will blur the condition present at impact." ],
  endings:{ overclaimWhat:"rx_sabotage", dismissalWhat:"rx_driver",
    win:{ expertTitle:"The Route Logic Reconstructed", expert:["You identify <b>Perren Voss — signalling infrastructure manager</b>, <b>The Infrastructure Head Office</b>, and <b>A bypassed interlock and deferred signalling maintenance</b>. Not sabotage — something left on the line. Not simple driver error — a signal run by. Track state, false clear, temporary strap, and deferred repair explain the collision authority.","Your finding shows that the express driver received a permissive condition created by infrastructure logic rather than simply ignoring a valid stop signal."], soundTitle:"A Fail-Safe Finding", sound:["You connect <b>Perren Voss — signalling infrastructure manager</b>, <b>The Infrastructure Head Office</b>, and <b>A bypassed interlock and deferred signalling maintenance</b>. The interlocking case is strong, although brake timing and crossing occupancy are summarized.","The rail panel accepts the result because relay tests, control logs, and maintenance notices independently reproduce the route state."], namedTitle:"The Bypassed Interlock Named", named:["You choose <b>Perren Voss — signalling infrastructure manager</b>, <b>The Infrastructure Head Office</b>, and <b>A bypassed interlock and deferred signalling maintenance</b>, but leave the exact transition from failed detection to false clear thin.","The accusation holds; safe reopening still requires a full test of route locking, detection, and temporary working."] },
    overclaim:{ title:"Sabotage Derails the Signal Evidence", body:["You select <b>Sabotage — something left on the line</b>, though an object or attacker does not explain the strapped interlock and permissive panel indication.","The sabotage story diverts attention from <b>A bypassed interlock and deferred signalling maintenance</b>, the signalling failure demonstrated by equipment and logs."] },
    dismissal:{ title:"Driver Blame Clears the Infrastructure", body:["You accept <b>Simple driver error — a signal run by</b>, treating the cab action as complete cause while the route system displayed authority it should have withheld.","That conclusion reopens the line with the same maintenance culture and temporary logic capable of producing another false clear."] },
    wrongNames:{ title:"Interlock Failure Correct, Route Custody Wrong", body:["You establish <b>A bypassed interlock and deferred signalling maintenance</b> but place the controlling records or manager incorrectly. The infrastructure chain identifies"] } },
